invariant: INV-17
file: src/aead_avx2.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh aead-avx2
reason: aead_avx2_seal returns without wiping its input words, eight of
  them the key, so its dead frame keeps the key side by side. Every tag
  is still right. bin/aead_avx2_equiv_test copies the stack below a seal
  and looks for the key; the script builds it for x86-64 and runs it
  under qemu-x86_64, because the file has a body there alone.

--- old
    hash_rest(&of_r, h, p, ct + hashed, n - hashed);
    ct_wipe(input, sizeof input);
--- new
    hash_rest(&of_r, h, p, ct + hashed, n - hashed);
